{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HiggsCategoricalMassFormula","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HiggsCategoricalMassFormula","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SubstrateEWHypotheses"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.higgs_W_Z_prediction_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.higgs_W_Z_prediction_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L196-L234","doc":"**The W- and Z-anchored predictions do NOT agree — they differ by\n`(P_3/P_2)^2`.**\n\nThis replaces a theorem that asserted outright equality,\n\n    m_W / m_Z = P_3/P_2  →  higgsMassFormula m_W h = higgsMassFromZ m_Z h,\n\nwhich is **false**. Substituting `m_W = m_Z · P_3/P_2` gives\n\n    LHS = m_Z · P_3 · P_4 · S / P_2^2      RHS = m_Z · P_4 · S / P_3,\n\nequal only when `P_3^2 = P_2^2`. They are not equal: `P_2 h = 1/2 + 3/2 h^2\n+ 1/2 h^4` and `P_3 h = 1/2 + 3 h^2 + 5/2 h^4 + 1/2 h^6` agree only at\n`h = 0` (both `1/2`); at `h = 1` they are `5/2` and `13/2`, a factor of\n`(13/5)^2 = 6.76` between the two predictions.\n\nThe old statement never compiled — the module was outside the `lake build`\nimport closure (bean qou-rc7b), and its proof (`field_simp; rw [hWZ]; ring`)\ndoes not go through. Patching the tactic would have been the wrong repair:\nthe proposition itself is not true.\n\nWhat *is* true is the exact discrepancy below, and it is the more useful\nstatement anyway — it says precisely how far apart the two anchors are, and\nso accounts for the numbers the old docstring quoted as evidence of\nagreement (m_W-prediction 124.26 vs m_Z-prediction 125.64, PR #1159: close,\nbut not equal, and the formula for the gap is exactly this). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.higgsMassFromZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.higgsMassFromZ","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L190-L194","doc":"Using m_W as anchor: m_H/m_W = (P_4/P_2) · (6/5) · (1 - h^4·2G).\nUsing m_Z as anchor: m_H/m_Z = (P_4/P_3) · (6/5) · (1 - h^4·2G).\nThe W and Z predictions should agree (both come from the same formula). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.scalar_gauge_ratio_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.scalar_gauge_ratio_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L160-L165","doc":"The scalar/gauge ratio at h = 0 is exactly 6/5 (no correction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tracePolynomial_2_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tracePolynomial_2_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L153-L158","doc":"Algebraic identity: P_2(0) = 1/2 (the c_0 coefficient at h=0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.h4_correction_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.h4_correction_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L147-L151","doc":"Trivial identity: at h = 0 (classical limit), the correction\nis exactly 1 (no h^4 contribution). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.vol_borromean_over_four_eq_two_catalan","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.vol_borromean_over_four_eq_two_catalan","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L139-L145","doc":"The h^4 correction's coefficient: Vol(B_3)/4 = 2G.\n\nDirect algebraic consequence of volBorromean = 8 · catalanG. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.six_fifths_eq_S3_over_partitions4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.six_fifths_eq_S3_over_partitions4","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L133-L137","doc":"The cardinality-ratio identity: 6/5 = |S_3| / |partitions(4)|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.higgsMassFormula","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.higgsMassFormula","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L119-L129","doc":"**The categorical Higgs mass formula** (CONSTRUCTED, PR #1159):\n\nm_H = m_W · (P_4(h)/P_2(h)) · (6/5) · (1 - h^4 · 2G)\n\nwhere:\nm_W is the W± mass (external SM anchor)\nP_m(h) is the binomial-pattern trace polynomial (sibling PR #1125)\n6/5 = |S_3|/|partitions(4)| (cardinality ratio)\n1 - h^4·2G is the h^4 structural correction (Vol(B_3) anchor) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.scalarOverGaugeRatio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.scalarOverGaugeRatio","kind":"def","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L112-L117","doc":"The categorical scalar-to-gauge mass-factor ratio.\n\nRefined identity from PR #1159: scalar/gauge = (6/5) · (1 - h^4 · 2G).\nEmpirically matches 171/143 to ~0.0025% (essentially exact). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.h4StructuralCorrection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.h4StructuralCorrection","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L103-L110","doc":"The h^4 structural correction factor: 1 - h^4 · Vol(B_3)/4 = 1 - h^4 · 2G.\n\nThis is the structural h^4 correction identified in PR #1159's\nsix_fifths_deviation_h4_correction_probe.py. It refines the\nleading 6/5 cardinality ratio with a higher-order term anchored\non the Borromean's hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.volBorromean","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.volBorromean","kind":"def","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L98-L101","doc":"Hyperbolic volume of the Borromean rings complement, Vol(𝓑_3) = 8G.\nAdams 1985 (cited via existing framework's `prop:vol-b3-eq-8g`).\nThe \"/4\" in the mass formula's correction = 2G. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.catalanG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.catalanG","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L69-L96","doc":"Catalan's constant G — referenced via the existing framework\nconvention (Vol(B_3) = 8G; Adams 1985). Real-valued, transcendental.\n\nImplementation note: encoded as a Real here for use in the mass\nformula; in production, this connects to mpmath G ≈ 0.91596.\n\n⚠ **NAME COLLISION + truncated-literal trap (flagged 2026-08-19).**\n\n1. This is a **decimal literal**, i.e. a rational — so the docstring's\n   \"transcendental\" describes the intended constant, not this definition.\n   Nothing in this file is false as a result: the only consequence drawn\n   from it, `volBorromean / 4 = 2 * catalanG`, is a `ring` identity that\n   holds for any value. But it is a live trap. The moment anyone asserts\n   `volBorromean = Vol(𝓑₃)`, or links it to\n   `QOU.Knot.BorromeanVolume`'s `8·Cl₂(π/2)`, that statement becomes\n   **false** — by ~1e-52 — in exactly the way `VOL_4_1` was before bean\n   `qou-yf47` replaced its truncated decimal with `2·Cl₂(π/3)`.\n2. A **second, different `catalanG`** exists in this corpus:\n   `QOU.Knot.WhiteheadVC.catalanG := ∑' n, (-1)^n/(2n+1)^2` — the exact\n   series. Two objects under one name is what the AGENTS.md notation\n   register forbids.\n\nThe exact form is already available: `QOU.Knot.clausen (π/2)`, with\ncertified rational bounds in `QOU/Knot/CatalanValueBounds.lean`. Switching\nto it is the `qou-yf47` repair applied here; left to this file's owner\nbecause it may move numerics downstream.\nAudit: `docs/audits/2026-08-19-volume-conjecture-work-overlap-sweep.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tracePolynomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tracePolynomial","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HiggsCategoricalMassFormula.lean#L47-L67","doc":"The trace polynomial $P_m(h)$ for $T(2, 2m)$ torus link.\n\nClosed form: $P_m(h) = \\sum_{j=0}^m \\binom{m+j}{2j} / 2 \\cdot h^{2j}$.\n\n**Provenance (cited):**\n- Sibling PR #1125 — sympy-verified the pattern for 54 cells (m=1..9, j=0..5)\n- Sibling PR #1165 — PROVED IN GENERAL via the Fibonacci-polynomial /\n  Chebyshev-of-second-kind identity (Graham–Knuth–Patashnik *Concrete\n  Mathematics* §6.6, Riordan *Combinatorial Identities* Ch 4 Eq 41a,\n  Vajda *Fibonacci and Lucas Numbers* §III.16)\n- PR #1174 (mine, merged, SUPERSEDED by #1165) — verified the\n  load-bearing Chebyshev identity $T_{2m+1}(x)/x = \\sum C(m+j, 2j) (4(x^2-1))^j$\n  symbolically for m = 0..6; that's now subsumed by #1165's general proof\n- PR #1185 — Lean encoding of the bar-symmetric/anti-symmetric structure\n\nThis noncomputable definition encodes the closed-form sum; actual\nevaluation requires the Real-arithmetic chain. The general-m proof\nlives in PR #1165's audit; this file consumes the closed form. ","signatureChunk":0}]}